TUvwWnl8EeBfEOpXklzZabq1jM0lpHMWQMwZkf5eVYYKkqRkN2xX9X1FVLhm6kvab\/AN3\/AIJTy2Nmk+vb\/gn8fvjzxLa658NtM1e5vtQtri3VL+eRh5s0wR3Cp5mSwVd5OFIBLZ4IJPy9491VtW8V6v4ivmlupbidlSF5GYj+EMznlsADrk1\/dHRXp4LKlh9pX+X\/AATqpYfkVrn8JOjX41XTMCxAmjG3esgAx\/PvWXrWjpaSo0q+X5gPTnd7V\/eVRXo+ys20zT2fmfwqeD9bTxvYaZ4avbm+lgtLh2sQWJhg3AFwQTkZx2Ff0E\/8GgHge28PaJ8dtWhubyWXW4fDfmRXEzTNF5X9qouGPYg9OwAr9oqKxjhWqimnoune44ws7n\/\/2Q==\u0022 width=\u0022310\u0022\u003E\u003C\/a\u003E\u003C\/span\u003E\u003C\/span\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoBodyText\u0022 style=\u0022margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:12px; margin-right:12px; margin-top:12px\u0022\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"ef47bb61-264f-4290-9399-5e482dc9c538","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/d3ef8742-594e-4e92-bb0d-0fbb09d855bd\/5299dbbe-f86d-44d4-91de-518c1565ca8e\/3e5980c9-309a-490e-8f07-058d594cecb8\/56493bee-511e-4745-ba70-6473a392884b","ref":{"parent":"3e5980c9-309a-490e-8f07-058d594cecb8","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h5"},"pos":"220-19-14-17","docId":"75","text":"French Country Style","id":"56493bee-511e-4745-ba70-6473a392884b","children":[{"path":"\/d3ef8742-594e-4e92-bb0d-0fbb09d855bd\/5299dbbe-f86d-44d4-91de-518c1565ca8e\/3e5980c9-309a-490e-8f07-058d594cecb8\/56493bee-511e-4745-ba70-6473a392884b\/b610aa7a-f688-431c-b5ae-3a32a8da14db","ref":{"parent":"56493bee-511e-4745-ba70-6473a392884b","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"220-19-14-17-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EDISTINGUISHING FEATURES\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFrench Country Style homes are characterized by steeply pitched roofs with eaves commonly flared upward at roof-wall junctions. They may be symmetrical in form and facade organization, but are more typically asymmetrical. Some variations include a round tower with a high, conical roof. Individual homes exhibit a wide variety in form detailing, but are united by the strong roof form. Roof are commonly covered with slate, tile or other rough-textured materials. Roof dormers are common. Entries are often deep-set from the home\u2019s front wall.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003EGable and hip roof forms with medium to steep pitch\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EClosed eaves\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EStucco, stone, or brick walls\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ERecessed entry vestibule with decorative molding or projecting gable\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EArticulated entry details\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ECasement windows with divided lights - often recessed\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ESecond floor overhangs with wood beam and decorative supports\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPlanter boxes, shutters, and other decorative details\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EDistinctive chimney shapes and caps\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EGabled dormers\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EBay windows with metal roofs\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoBodyText\u0022 style=\u0022margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:12px; margin-right:12px; margin-top:12px\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-size:12pt\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-family:Cambria,serif\u0022\u003E\u003Ca\u003E\u003Cimg alt=\u0022\u0022 height=\u0022264\u0022 src=\u0022data:image\/jpeg;base64,\/9j\/4AAQSkZJRgABAQEAYABgAAD\/2wBDAAIBAQIBAQICAgICAgICAwUDAwMDAwYEBAMFBwYHBwcGBwcICQsJCAgKCAcHCg0KCgsMDAwMBwkODw0MDgsMDAz\/2wBDAQICAgMDAwYDAwYMCAcIDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAz\/wAARCAFiAYMDASIAAhEBAxEB\/8QAHwAAAQUBAQEBAQEAAAAAAAAAAAECAwQFBgcICQoL\/8QAtRAAAgEDAwIEAwUFBAQAAAF9AQIDAAQRBRIhMUEGE1FhByJxFDKBkaEII0KxwRVS0fAkM2JyggkKFhcYGRolJicoKSo0NTY3ODk6Q0RFRkdISUpTVFVWV1hZWmNkZWZnaGlqc3R1dnd4eXqDhIWGh4iJipKTlJWWl5iZmqKjpKWmp6ipqrKztLW2t7i5usLDxMXGx8jJytLT1NXW19jZ2uHi4+Tl5ufo6erx8vP09fb3+Pn6\/8QAHwEAAwEBAQEBAQEBAQAAAAAAAAECAwQFBgcICQoL\/8QAtREAAgECBAQDBAcFBAQAAQJ3AAECAxEEBSExBhJBUQdhcRMiMoEIFEKRobHBCSMzUvAVYnLRChYkNOEl8RcYGRomJygpKjU2Nzg5OkNERUZHSElKU1RVVldYWVpjZGVmZ2hpanN0dXZ3eHl6goOEhYaHiImKk